ent is replaced with the newly discovered definition, and an auto-discovered id that stops appearing is removed. Explicitly configured inventory entries are preserved and are not replaced or removed by discovery (see [Configuration precedence](#configuration-precedence)).\n\n## Configuration precedence\n\nCanopy resolves configuration in this order:\n\n1. `-config <path>` — load exactly that inventory file. A missing or invalid file is a fatal startup error.\n2. `./canopy.json` — loaded when `-config` is not set and the file exists. A present but invalid default file is skipped.\n3. Zero-config discovery — when no inventory file is loaded, Canopy starts with an empty inventory. Discovery then runs at startup and periodically (see [Discovery](#discovery)).\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788549544964},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me rebase the branch onto master f2c0e7b. Then fix the README bullet. Let me rebase.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"Now let me rebase the branch onto master f2c0e7b. Then fix the README bullet. Let me rebase.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"Now let me rebase the branch onto master `f2c0e7b`:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_98835cacb9814f3d91532d8b","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/phaedrus/development/misty-step/canopy/.forest/worktrees/1788549506905489060-fixer && git rebase f2c0e7b 2>&1 | tail -10 && echo \"---LOG---\" && git log --oneline -8 && echo \"---STATUS---\" && git status --short"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731","usage":{"input":497,"output":167,"cacheRead":19456,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":23,"totalTokens":20120,"cost":{"input":0.00002485,"output":0.000016700000000000003,"cacheRead":0.00019456,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00023611000000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788549544965,"responseId":"gen-1788549544-95cfgD0CyFFmxFakjUtO","rawStop